    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner's tier becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nChanges, following the existing Spring/MapStruct conventions:\n\n1. **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `countHouseholdMembers(String householdId)`, a read-only method that counts owners sharing a given non-null `householdId` (returns 0 for null), mirroring the existing `findAll()`-iteration style used by `assignHousehold`/`isHouseholdInUse`.\n\n2. **`Owner`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` `householdMemberCount` field (with accessors). It's not persisted, since household size can change over time; it carries the freshly-counted size into the DTO mapping, alongside the already-derived fields like `namesakeCount`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.toMembershipTier`** \u2014 now returns `GOLD` first when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, then falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 populates `householdMemberCount` (via the new service method) before mapping to the DTO in both `addOwner` (after save, so the count reflects the state \"after this create\") and `getOwner`, so the tier is correct on both the create response and subsequent reads.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`) and the full suite pass.",
