        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and consistent with how this codebase is already organized:\n\n- **Tier logic stays in the mapper.** The GOLD clause is added to `OwnerMapper.toMembershipTier`, which already houses the SILVER/BRONZE derivation. This is exactly the right unit \u2014 tier derivation is not scattered into a new place, and the Javadoc is updated to match.\n\n- **The transient field mirrors the existing sibling.** `Owner.householdMemberCount` (`@Transient`, with plain getter/setter) is structurally identical to the existing `namesakeCount` field that feeds the same `toMembershipTier` method. A maintainer would find this immediately familiar.\n\n- **`countHouseholdMembers` sits naturally with the other household logic.** `ClinicService` already owns the household cluster (`isHouseholdInUse`, `assignHousehold`, and `householdId` assignment). Placing a household-member count next to them is a coherent domain grouping, and it's genuinely shared by two call sites (`getOwner` and `addOwner`), which justifies a service method over an inline helper. The interface + impl addition follows the established `@Override` / `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` pattern of its neighbors.\n\n- **The `findAll()` iteration matches the codebase's established style,** not a new smell \u2014 `isHouseholdInUse`, `assignHousehold`, `countNamesakes`, and `countOwnersInCity` all count/scan via `findAll()` rather than a derived repository query. It compares by `householdId` directly (correctly not reusing the `sameHousehold` normalization machinery, since ids are already assigned), so there is no duplication.\n\nOne very minor observation (not blocking): the two-line `setHouseholdMemberCount(countHouseholdMembers(...))` call is repeated in `getOwner` and `addOwner`, but the parallel `namesakeCount` code isn't abstracted either, so leaving it inline is the locally consistent choice. Structure is clean."
